{"id": "86338", "name": "אינטגרל מוכלל מסוג שני – 1/x^(n/(n+1)) מ-0 (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Evaluate the following improper integral if possible.</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\int^{{CT:0}}_0 \\frac{1}{{{CT:1}}^\\frac{{CT:2}}{{CT:3}}}\\, d{{CT:1}} \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">[[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-size:0.92em;color:#555;margin:6px 0 0\">If the integral cannot be evaluated enter 99999 (5 9's).</p></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Write the integral as a limit at the point where the integrand is unbounded, integrate with the power rule, and take the limit.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — Writing the integral as a limit</b><br>The integrand <span dir=\"ltr\">\\({{CT:4}}\\)</span> is unbounded near <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(0\\)</span>, so by definition<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\int_0^{{{CT:0}}} {{CT:4}}\\,dx=\\lim_{\\varepsilon\\to0^+}\\int_{\\varepsilon}^{{{CT:0}}} {{CT:4}}\\,dx \\]</p>This is a power integral <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(\\int_0^{c} x^{-p}\\,dx\\)</span> with <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(p={{CT:5}}\\)</span>; since <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(p&lt;1\\)</span>, it converges.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — An antiderivative</b><br>By the power rule (add one to the exponent and divide by the new exponent):<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\int {{CT:4}}\\,dx={{CT:6}}+C \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 3 — The limit</b><br><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\int_{\\varepsilon}^{{{CT:0}}} {{CT:4}}\\,dx={{CT:7}}-{{CT:3}}\\,\\varepsilon^{{{CT:8}}} \\]</p>As <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(\\varepsilon\\to0^+\\)</span>, <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(\\varepsilon^{{{CT:8}}}\\to 0\\)</span>, so the lower limit contributes <span dir=\"ltr\">\\({{CT:9}}\\)</span>:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[\\int^{{CT:0}}_0 {{CT:4}} d{{CT:1}} = \\left[{{CT:6}}\\right]^{{CT:0}}_0 = {{CT:7}}-{{CT:9}} = {{CT:10}}\\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 20, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "integrate", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 2, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "correctanswer", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-0-T ", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "Result-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "derivlimits", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-1-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">It looks like you may have differentiated instead!</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-1-F ", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["J", "Jindefinite", "correctanswer", "deriv", "deriv2", "derivlimits", "f", "lowerJ", "n1", "n2", "n3", "upperJ", "v"], "nvariants": 9}